## Why these settings (Keycloak 26, no legacy)

This client was scaffolded with non-legacy defaults. The following flags are off **by design**:

- `implicit_flow_enabled = false` — implicit grant is deprecated in OAuth 2.1; tokens leak through URL fragments.
- `direct_access_grants_enabled = false` — Resource Owner Password Credentials is deprecated; the user's password reaches the client app and defeats SSO.
{%- if client_type == "public" %}
- `pkce_code_challenge_method = "S256"` — PKCE is mandatory for public clients to prevent authorization-code interception. `plain` is not used.
{%- endif %}
- `client_secret` is not committed — Keycloak generates it on apply; DevOps delivers it out-of-band.

If the application genuinely needs any of these legacy options (e.g., a CLI tool that can only do device-code or ROPC), raise an exception with the SSO platform team **before** flipping the flag in the MR. Do not silently re-enable.

